  "query_preview": "..\n(Monday Night through next Sunday)\nIssued at 1123 AM CDT Sun May 17 2026\n\nBeneficial rains are in the forecast for mid week, mainly Tuesday\nafternoon through Wednesday, as the synoptic ridge suppresses\nsomewhat to our southeast. This will provide more access for\nshortwaves to advance across the region with favorable \nmoisture/instability along a cold front. Showers and \nthunderstorms are expected with best chances during peak diurnal \nheating, especially on Wednesday. Severe weather chances remain \nlow overall, but not completely zero, due to the tendency for \nstorms to form into line segments which may pose a damaging wind \nthreat. Additional isolated severe weather may be possible on \nWednesday as well, but the overall environment may become more \nmessy/less unstable and best bulk shear is forecast to remain \nwell to our northwest, which is not unusual this time of year. \nOverall rain amounts of 1-2\" are forecast Tuesday and Wednesday \nwith locally higher amounts.\n\nMedium-range guidance is suggestive of the weakened front \nstalling somewhere in the region with southwesterly flow aloft \nand moisture advection persisting. This would support waves of \nshowers and thunderstorms with any subsequent shortwave \ndisturbances. Though details are less predictable this far out, \nthis is a favored synoptic setup for continued chances of \nbeneficial rains to our drought-worn area. An additional inch or \ntwo of rain would be possible late week into the weekend if this \nworks out.",
